## Database Setup

This project uses **Prisma** as the ORM. Available commands:

```bash
{{#if isPnpm}}pnpm prisma:generate{{else if isYarn}}yarn prisma:generate{{else if isBun}}bun run prisma:generate{{else}}npm run prisma:generate{{/if}}
{{#if isPnpm}}pnpm prisma:push{{else if isYarn}}yarn prisma:push{{else if isBun}}bun run prisma:push{{else}}npm run prisma:push{{/if}}
{{#if isPnpm}}pnpm prisma:studio{{else if isYarn}}yarn prisma:studio{{else if isBun}}bun run prisma:studio{{else}}npm run prisma:studio{{/if}}
{{#if isPnpm}}pnpm prisma:migrate{{else if isYarn}}yarn prisma:migrate{{else if isBun}}bun run prisma:migrate{{else}}npm run prisma:migrate{{/if}}
{{#if isPnpm}}pnpm prisma:migrate:deploy{{else if isYarn}}yarn prisma:migrate:deploy{{else if isBun}}bun run prisma:migrate:deploy{{else}}npm run prisma:migrate:deploy{{/if}}
```
{{#if hasSqlserver}}

Set `SQLSERVER_HOST`, `SQLSERVER_PORT`, `SQLSERVER_DATABASE`, `SQLSERVER_USER`, and `SQLSERVER_PASSWORD` in `.env` before running Prisma commands. The SQL Server database must already exist. The generated password is a development-only example that satisfies SQL Server's password policy; replace it with a unique secret before sharing the project or deploying it. For local development, set `SQLSERVER_TRUST_SERVER_CERTIFICATE=true` when using a self-signed certificate; keep certificate validation enabled for production.
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

